  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INSTITUTO SOCIOAMBIENTAL 2023 GRANT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This funding will support the Brazilian NGO Instituto Socioambiental (ISA) to implement the project &#x2018;Technology, information and new models of governance for the protection of traditional territories&#x2019;, with a grant of &#x20ac;600,000 for one year. This is Irish Aid&#x2019;s second contribution to ISA (&#x20ac;270,000 in 2022), and will be governed by a one-year contract. This is funding for the second year of an initial three year programme. Additional funding has been earmarked for 2024. ISA is a highly regarded NGO in Brazil that has been working in the Rio Negro and Xingu regions for over 30 years, and is considered a reference in terms of their direct actions to support the territories and their role as a national advocate for environmental protection and the rights of Indigenous peoples.</narrative>
  </description>
